Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The algebra", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The key algebraic facts about ",
  StyleBox["PD", "InlineInput"],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["PE", "InlineInput"],
  " are that both operations are ",
  StyleBox["bilinear",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", and the latter is also ",
  StyleBox["skew symmetric",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ".  We can verify these algebraic properties by ",
  StyleBox["symbolic computation",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ".  Let us enter first some ",
  StyleBox["general forms",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " with ",
  StyleBox["symbolic coefficients",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(p\_1 = a\_1\ u + a\_2\ v + a\_3\ w; \n
    p\_2 = b\_1\ u + b\_2\ v + b\_3\ w; \np\_3 = c\_1\ u + c\_2\ v + c\_3\ w; 
    \)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(l\_1 = d\_1\ x + d\_2\ y + d\_3\ z; \n
    l\_2 = e\_1\ x + e\_2\ y + e\_3\ z; \nl\_3 = f\_1\ x + f\_2\ y + f\_3\ z; 
    \)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Now, checking that ",
  StyleBox["PD", "InlineInput"],
  " is bilinear in the ",
  StyleBox["first argument",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " comes down to this:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[h\ l\_1 + k\ l\_2, p\_1] == 
        h\ PD[l\_1, p\_1] + k\ PD[\ l\_2, p\_1] // ExpandAll\)], "Input"],

Cell["We then check the second argument:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[l\_1, h\ p\_1 + k\ p\_2] == 
        h\ PD[l\_1, p\_1] + k\ PD[\ l\_1, p\_2] // ExpandAll\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We also do the corresponding checks for ",
  StyleBox["PE", "InlineInput"],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PE[h\ p\_1 + k\ p\_2, p\_3] == 
        h\ PE[p\_1, p\_3] + k\ PE[\ p\_2, p\_3] // ExpandAll\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PE[p\_1, h\ p\_2 + k\ p\_3] == 
        h\ PE[p\_1, p\_2] + k\ PE[\ p\_1, p\_3] // ExpandAll\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PE[h\ l\_1 + k\ l\_2, l\_3] == 
        h\ PE[l\_1, l\_3] + k\ PE[\ l\_2, l\_3] // ExpandAll\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PE[l\_1, h\ l\_2 + k\ l\_3] == 
        h\ PE[l\_1, l\_2] + k\ PE[\ l\_1, l\_3] // ExpandAll\)], "Input"],

Cell["We can also check skew symmetry:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\ PE[p\_1, p\_2] == \(-PE[p\_2, p\_1]\)\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Inasmuch as ",
  StyleBox["0", "InlineInput"],
  " is the only number equal to its own negative, we conclude from the skew \
symmetry property together with bilinearity that:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\ PE[p\_1, h\ p\_1] == 0\  // ExpandAll\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "What is interesting, of course, is that the ",
  StyleBox["only forms",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " satisfying ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(PE[p\_1, p\_2] == \ 0\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " are the forms ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(p\_2 == \ h\ p\_1\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "  for some scalar ",
  StyleBox["h", "InlineInput"],
  " \[LongDash] provided ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(p\_1\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "is not ",
  StyleBox["0", "InlineInput"],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Inasmuch as the triple combination below comes out to be the \
evaluation of a 3x3 determinant, here is another kind of skew symmetry we can \
check:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    StyleBox[
      \(PD[PE[p\_1, p\_2], p\_3] == \(-PD[PE[p\_1, p\_3], p\_2]\) // ExpandAll
        \),
      FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
And remember to clear assignments when you are finished with \
them.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ClearAll[Subscript]\)], "Input"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData["Desargues\[CloseCurlyQuote] Theorem"], "Subsection",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A proof by symbolic computation", "Subsubsection",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Theorem.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " If two triangles are ",
  StyleBox["perspective",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " from a common point, then ",
  StyleBox["the intersections of corresponding sides",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " are ",
  StyleBox["collinear",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "."
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0]],

Cell["\<\
Here is a picture (which we will show how to compute later) which \
illustrates the theorem. \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
