J@000?l0J@000?l0J@000001\
\>"],
  ImageRangeCache->{{{0, 359}, {359, 0}} -> {-15.1668, -14.8335, 0.102137, 
  0.102137}}],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We are going to carry out the proof of the theorem by ",
  StyleBox["symbolic computation",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " (",
  StyleBox["i.e.",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", using algebra) with the aid of the operations ",
  StyleBox["PD ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["PE ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "applied to linear forms representing points and lines."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "As we pointed out, the problem of finding the point that is  ",
  StyleBox["the intersection of two lines",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " each determined by ",
  StyleBox["joining",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " two of their points may be calculated as follows:"
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ClearAll[a, b, c]; \n\n
    PE[PE[a\_1\ u + a\_2\ v + a\_3\ w, b\_1\ u + b\_2\ v + b\_3\ w], 
        PE[c\_1\ u + c\_2\ v + c\_3\ w, d\_1\ u + d\_2\ v + d\_3\ w]] // Tidy
      \)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Note that the answer here is much more ",
  StyleBox["symmetric",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " than the answer found previously just using vector algebra.  This perhaps \
shows the virtue of homogeneous coordinates \[LongDash] which also have \
another virtue of not requiring distinctions between parallel and \
non-parallel lines.  "
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof of the Theorem.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "Consider a triangle and a point not on any one of the three sides.  As we \
will prove later, such a configuration can always be moved to a ",
  StyleBox["standard position",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ".  We assume this now, so as to cut down on the algebraic computations."
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Let us therefore take the ",
  StyleBox["special point",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " ",
  StyleBox["OO", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "(for the center of the perspectivity) at the ",
  StyleBox["origin",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " (namely, the point  ",
  StyleBox["w", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "when the line ",
  StyleBox["z", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "is taken to be the line at infinity).  Next, the  ",
  StyleBox["vertices",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of the triangle are the two ",
  StyleBox["unit points",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " on the axes together with the ",
  StyleBox["point completing the square",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ".  We will call this \"standard\" triangle ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\({A\_1, B\_1, C\_1}\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "."
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  "On the lines joining the origin to the vertices of the triangle, we next \
chose three ",
  StyleBox["arbitrarily placed points ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "(but all ",
  StyleBox["different from",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " the point ",
  StyleBox["w", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ") forming a triangle ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\({A\_2, B\_2, C\_2}\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ".  We thus have our two triangles ",
  StyleBox["perspective",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "  from the point ",
  StyleBox["w",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " using the three lines ",
  StyleBox["x", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["y", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["x-y", "InlineInput"],
  ".  "
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We may enter this information into ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "  as follows: "
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(OO = w; \nA\_1 = u + w; \ \ \ B\_1 = v + w; \ \ \ \ C\_1 = u + v + w; \n
    A\_2 = u + a\ w; B\_2 = v + b\ w; C\_2 = u + v + c\ w; \)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The theorem of Desargues invites us to look at the three points that are ",
  
  StyleBox["the intersections of the corresponding sides",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ":"
}], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(D\_1 = PE[PE[A\_1, B\_1], PE[A\_2, B\_2]] // Tidy; \n
    D\_2 = PE[PE[B\_1, C\_1], PE[B\_2, C\_2]] // Tidy; \n
    D\_3 = PE[PE[C\_1, A\_1], PE[C\_2, A\_2]] // Tidy; 
    \n{D\_1, \ D\_2, \ D\_3}\  // \ TableForm\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We can see that if ",
  StyleBox["two",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of the quantities ",
  StyleBox["a",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["b",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", or ",
  StyleBox["c",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  are ",
  StyleBox["both",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " equal to ",
  StyleBox["1",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", then at least one of these points degenerates to ",
  StyleBox["0",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", which is ",
  StyleBox["not",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " a (representative of a) point.   By the choice of the notation for the \
points, the equation ",
  StyleBox["a == 1",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", for instance, means that we have ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(A\_1\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[" == ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(A\_2\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  So we have to ",
  StyleBox["assume",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " additionally that",
  StyleBox[" ",
    Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0]],
  StyleBox["the two triangles share at most one vertex in common",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic",
    Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Now we ",
  StyleBox["check",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " whether the three points are ",
  StyleBox["collinear",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[PE[D\_1, D\_2], D\_3]\)], "Input"],

Cell["Hmmmm.  That does not look good.  Are they collinear or not?", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Expand[%]\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["They are! ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " That ",
  StyleBox["proves",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " the theorem (for the points in that special position) by symbolic \
computation.  ",
  StyleBox["Q.E.D.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Finding a formula", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We did much computation in carrying out the proof.  So, let's now try to \
find the ",
  StyleBox["formula",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " for the Desargues line.  There are three ways to define it.  And they \
look better when factored and collected:"
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Des\_1 = Tidy/@Factor[PE[D\_2, D\_3]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Des\_2 = Tidy/@Factor[PE[D\_1, D\_3]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Des\_3 = Tidy/@Factor[PE[D\_1, D\_2]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "By assumption, at least two of the factors ",
  StyleBox["(a - 1)",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["(b - 1)",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", and ",
  StyleBox["(c - 1)",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " are not ",
  StyleBox["0",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", so the formula we seek is:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Des\_4 = 
      \((b - c)\)\ x + \((a - c)\)\ y + \((\(-a\) - b + c + 1)\)\ z; \)\)], 
  "Input"],

Cell[TextData[
"Here is a drawing of one version of the configuration."], "Text",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(a = 1\/4; b = 1\/3; c = 1\/7; \), 
    \(\(Draw[{{OO, "\<O\>"}, \n
        \t\t{A\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_1\)\>\""}, {B\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_1\)\>\""}, {
          C\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_1\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{A\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_2\)\>\""}, {B\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_2\)\>\""}, {
          C\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_2\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{D\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(D\_1\)\>\""}, {D\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(D\_2\)\>\""}, {
          D\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(D\_3\)\>\""}, \n\t\tPE[OO, A\_1], PE[OO, B\_1], 
        PE[OO, C\_1], \n\t\tPE[A\_1, B\_1], PE[A\_2, B\_2], \n\t\t
        PE[B\_1, C\_1], PE[B\_2, C\_2], \n\t\tPE[C\_1, A\_1], PE[C\_2, A\_2], 
        \n\t\tDes\_4}]; \)\)}], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
We can also skew the axes (a process we will understand better when \
we study projective transformations).\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(a = 1\/2; b = 1\/3; c = 1\/4; \n
    Draw[{{OO, "\<O\>"}, \n
        \t\t{A\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_1\)\>\""}, {B\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_1\)\>\""}, {
          C\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_1\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{A\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_2\)\>\""}, {B\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_2\)\>\""}, {
          C\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_2\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{D\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(D\_1\)\>\""}, {D\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(D\_2\)\>\""}, {
          D\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(D\_3\)\>\""}, \n\t\tPE[OO, A\_1], PE[OO, B\_1], 
        PE[OO, C\_1], \n\t\tPE[A\_1, B\_1], PE[A\_2, B\_2], \n\t\t
        PE[B\_1, C\_1], PE[B\_2, C\_2], \n\t\tPE[C\_1, A\_1], PE[C\_2, A\_2], 
        \n\t\tDes\_4}, \n\t\ \ 
      To\  -> \ {\(-u\) - v + 5  w, 3  u + w, \ 2  v + w, z}]; \)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ClearAll[a, b, c, Subscript]\)], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A proof by pictures", "Subsubsection",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False,
  AnimationCycleOffset->0.0625,
  AnimationCycleRepetitions->Infinity],

Cell["\<\
Here is an (old version) of an animated picture showing what \
happens as vertices are moved.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
