Cell[TextData[{
  "Look again at the picture and imagine the ",
  StyleBox["blue",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["green",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 1, 0]],
  " triangles sitting up ",
  StyleBox["in space",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ".  They each determine a ",
  StyleBox["plane",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", and imagine that the planes are different.  Two planes will intersect in \
a ",
  StyleBox["line",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " \[LongDash] namely, the ",
  StyleBox["red",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
  " line.  But, the intersections of corresponding sides \[LongDash] namely, \
of one ",
  StyleBox["blue",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
  " line and one ",
  StyleBox["green",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 1, 0]],
  " line \[LongDash] will lie on ",
  StyleBox["both",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " planes.  Therefore, the points all lie on that ",
  StyleBox["red",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
  " line.  In other words, in space, the proof of the theorem uses only the \
most basic properties of incidence of points, lines, and planes."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Thus,",
    FontWeight->"Plain",
    FontSlant->"Plain"],
  " if",
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["we could argue in space, ",
    FontWeight->"Plain",
    FontSlant->"Plain"],
  "then",
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox[
  "this is a perfectly good proof when the triangles are not flat.  The whole \
proof could then be completed by remarking that a flat picture is always a ",
    FontWeight->"Plain",
    FontSlant->"Plain"],
  "projection",
  StyleBox[" of a 3D-picture.  But this approach requires the use of space.",
    FontWeight->"Plain",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData["Pappus\[CloseCurlyQuote] Theorem"], "Subsection",
  CellMargins->{{Inherited, 73}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The theorem", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Theorem",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ". If a hexagon is placed with alternate vertices on two lines, then the \
intersections of the three pair of opposite sides are collinear."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "To simplify the algebra, we take the points placed on the ",
  StyleBox["x",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["y",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " axes.  (By the use of projective transformations, this is not a loss of \
generality \[LongDash] as we will argue later).  Otherwise, we take arbitrary \
such points."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(A\_1 = a\_1\ u + b\_1\ w; \nA\_2 = a\_2\ u + b\_2\ w; \n
    A\_3 = a\_3\ u + b\_3\ w; \nB\_1 = c\_1\ v + d\_1\ w; \n
    B\_2 = c\_2\ v + d\_2\ w; \nB\_3 = c\_3\ v + d\_3\ w; \)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Following the statement of the theorem, we intersect the line joining the \
points ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(A\_2\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " and  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(B\_3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " with the line joining ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(A\_3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(B\_2\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " (and similarly for the other pairs)."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(C\_1 = PE[PE[A\_2, B\_3], PE[A\_3, B\_2]] // Tidy; \n
    C\_2 = PE[PE[A\_1, B\_3], PE[A\_3, B\_1]] // Tidy; \n
    C\_3 = PE[PE[A\_1, B\_2], PE[A\_2, B\_1]] // Tidy; \)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData["Let us take a look at a couple of the points."], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(C\_1\)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(C\_2\)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[
"They are not too bad.  What about the line joining these two points?"], 
  "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(pappus = PE[C\_1, C\_2] // Tidy\)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Hmmmmmmmm!  That last formula is rather ",
  StyleBox["heavy",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ".  Perhaps the expression can be ",
  StyleBox["factored",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell["pappus = Tidy/@Factor[pappus]", "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Good!  We found the common factor ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[
        RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["a", 
            StyleBox["3",
              FontWeight->"Bold"]], \(c\_3\)}],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "; so it can be dropped:"
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(pappus = pappus\/\(a\_3\ c\_3\) // Tidy\)], "Input",
  PageBreakAbove->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  "That looks much better.  Finally, let us see whether the point ",
  StyleBox["C3",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " lies on this line."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  PageBreakAbove->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Expand[PD[pappus, C\_3]]\)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["It does!",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "  So that proves the theorem \[LongDash] provided the dropping of the \
factor was justified.  "
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[TextData[{
  "But, in this arrangement of points, the condition ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\(a\_3\) c\_3 == 0\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "means that either the vertex ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(A\_3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " or the vertex ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(B\_3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " is at the origin ",
  StyleBox["w", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  Now this is clearly a ",
  StyleBox["degenerate situation",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", so it is fair to assume that none of the vertices of the hexagon are at \
the intersection of the given pair of lines.  ",
  StyleBox["Q.E.D.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Some diagrams", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
We show two illustrations, one without and one with the sides of \
the hexagon drawn in.  Other pictures can be obtained by altering the \
parameters.\
\>", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(a\_1 = 2; \ \ \ \ b\_1 = 1; \na\_2 = 4; \ \ \ \ b\_2 = 1; \na\_3 = 8; 
    \ \ \ \ b\_3 = 1; \nc\_1 = 1; \ \ \ \ d\_1 = 1; \nc\_2 = 2; \ \ \ \ 
    d\_2 = 1; \nc\_3 = 5; \ \ \ \ d\_3 = 1; \n\t
    Draw[{x, y, pappus, \n
        \t\t{A\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_1\)\>\""}, {A\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_2\)\>\""}, {
          A\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_3\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{B\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_1\)\>\""}, {B\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_2\)\>\""}, {
          B\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_3\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{C\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_1\)\>\""}, {C\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_2\)\>\""}, {
          C\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_3\)\>\""}}]; \)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Draw[{x, y, pappus, \n
        \t\t{A\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_1\)\>\""}, {A\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_2\)\>\""}, {
          A\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(A\_3\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{B\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_1\)\>\""}, {B\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_2\)\>\""}, {
          B\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(B\_3\)\>\""}, \n
        \t\t{C\_1, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_1\)\>\""}, {C\_2, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_2\)\>\""}, {
          C\_3, \*"\"\<\!\(C\_3\)\>\""}, \n\t\tPE[A\_2, B\_3], 
        PE[A\_3, B\_2], \n\t\tPE[A\_1, B\_3], PE[A\_3, B\_1], \n\t\t
        PE[A\_1, B\_2], PE[A\_2, B\_1]}]; \)\)], "Input",
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

